Your goal is to analyse an existing iOS (and, where present, macOS) in-app purchase test and produce a concrete plan for adding a UWP variant. You do **not** write or edit any files. Pseudo-code is allowed in the plan for clarity.

## Important — platform-split is intentional

iOS, macOS and UWP tests live as **separate `test_{id}_*_ios` / `test_{id}_*_mac` / `test_{id}_*_uwp` functions in the same file**, even when QASE describes a single scenario. Each platform may legitimately behave differently (UI, Microsoft Store flow, networking, engine response timing) — the split lets each test follow the actual platform behaviour rather than papering over it with `if PLATFORM_TO_RUN` guards or "tolerant" assertions. Divergence is acceptable; document it inline (`# TODO`, comment, or a Known-patterns note) when it appears.

The macOS variant is usually the most complete reference (it already covers crash, network-loss, clock-shift and Amplitude scenarios). **Read both the iOS and macOS functions** before planning the UWP one — the macOS test is often a closer structural match than iOS because both are desktop/local.

